## Part 2: The Production Architecture

### Target Pipeline

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Layer 0: Data Pipeline"
        A[Multi-Source Ingest<br/>Wikipedia/PDF/Custom] --> B[Chunking + Cleaning]
        B --> C[Embedding Model<br/>sentence-transformers]
        C --> D[FAISS Vector Store]
    end
    
    subgraph "Layer 1: Retrieval (RAG)"
        E[User Query] --> F[Query Embedding]
        F --> G[FAISS Top-K Search]
        G --> H[Context Assembly]
    end
    
    subgraph "Layer 2: Reasoning (LLM)"
        H --> I[Prompt Template]
        I --> J[Transformer Backbone<br/>Phi-3.5-mini / Mistral-7B]
        J --> K[Generated Response]
    end
    
    subgraph "Layer 3: Brain Regions"
        K --> L[PFC: Chain-of-Thought]
        K --> M[LH: Factual Grounding]
        K --> N[RH: Creative Synthesis]
        K --> O[HC: Memory Store]
    end
    
    subgraph "Layer 4: Serving"
        P[FastAPI Server]
        Q[Gradio UI]
    end
```

### Technology Choices (T4-Compatible)

| Component | Technology | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **LLM Backbone** | `microsoft/Phi-3.5-mini-instruct` (3.8B) | Fits in T4 16GB with 4-bit quantization + LoRA. Best quality/size ratio. |
| **Fine-Tuning** | QLoRA (4-bit NF4 + LoRA rank 16) | 4.2GB VRAM for training. Proven production technique. |
| **Embeddings** | `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2` | 80MB model, 384-dim vectors. Fast enough for real-time RAG. |
| **Vector Store** | FAISS (IVFFlat) | CPU-compatible, scales to millions of vectors, zero dependencies. |
| **Serving** | FastAPI + Gradio | Industry standard. Gradio gives instant UI. |
| **Training Framework** | HuggingFace Transformers + PEFT + TRL | The entire ML industry uses this stack. |

