## Part 5: What to Keep from the Current Architecture

> [!TIP]
> The 4-region brain metaphor is actually a **strong architectural idea** when backed by real models.

| Current Concept | How It Survives in v2 |
|---|---|
| **4 Brain Regions (LH/RH/PFC/HC)** | Become **prompt routing modes** — PFC uses chain-of-thought, LH uses citation-heavy prompts, RH uses creative/lateral prompts, HC stores conversation memory |
| **Curiosity / Joy / Fear emotions** | Become **generation temperature modifiers** — high curiosity → higher temperature, fear → lower temperature + more conservative retrieval |
| **Brain Shards (.para files)** | Become **FAISS index partitions** — each region has its own vector subspace |
| **Associative Memory (HC)** | Becomes **graph-based topic linking** on top of FAISS — real episodic memory |
| **ManifoldScrubber** | Becomes the **pre-processing pipeline** for RAG context assembly |
| **Bootstrap Q&A Pairs** | Become the **seed fine-tuning dataset** for QLoRA training |

